Fingerprint database
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The fingerprint database is licensed Apache-2.0 rather than MIT, because it is
a compilation that aggregates material under BSD-3-Clause, MIT and Apache-2.0
terms. Apache-2.0 absorbs all three coherently; MIT cannot relabel Apache-2.0
material.

Signals currently shipped were written from publicly documented vendor response
patterns and are not derived from another project's source.

Upstream databases approved for systematic import, with the attribution each
requires. Every imported entry records its origin in a per-entry `source` field.

  WAFW00F - https://github.com/EnableSecurity/wafw00f
    Copyright (c) 2009-2026 WAFW00F Developers. BSD-3-Clause.

  identYwaf - https://github.com/stamparm/identYwaf              MIT
  cdncheck - https://github.com/projectdiscovery/cdncheck        MIT
  wafme0w - https://github.com/Lu1sDV/wafme0w                    MIT
  nuclei-templates - https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates
                                                                 MIT
  Awesome-WAF - https://github.com/0xInfection/Awesome-WAF        Apache-2.0
  Vxscan - https://github.com/al0ne/Vxscan                        Apache-2.0

EXCLUDED - do not import:

  WhatWaf - https://github.com/Ekultek/WhatWaf                    GPL
    Copyleft; cannot be relicensed into this compilation. Individual header
    names are uncopyrightable facts, but a curated compilation of them is
    protected. Where WhatWaf covers a vendor no permissive source does, treat
    that vendor as a research target and derive signals independently.

  JA4+ (JA4S and related) - https://github.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4
    FoxIO License 1.1. JA4 (client) is BSD-3-Clause, but JA4S - the server-side
    fingerprint relevant here - is not permissive for monetization. Deferred.
